  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through next Thursday)\nIssued at 1219 PM CDT Fri Oct 30 2026\n\nShort wave ridging will move overhead from late Saturday through \nSunday in advance of a deep trough on the west coast. Southerly \nmoist flow will allow for a quick return of low stratus Saturday \nnight into Sunday morning. Height falls will move overhead late in \nthe day on Sunday as the trough tracks across the Rockies. Large \nscale ascent will spread overhead during this time and provide a \nquick shot of precipitation through Monday morning. Areas of lift \nwill favor the extreme southern Texas Panhandle into northern \nportions of the South Plains before subsidence moves overhead later \non Monday. A couple of cold fronts will also affect the area from \nthis system. The first cold front will be during the day on Monday \nas a pacific cold front shifting breezy winds to the west and \nadvecting drier air into the region.",
